---
kind: lore
id: ledger
title: The torn ledger and the men who kept it
series: wardLedger
---

<entry id="ledgerPage1" on="read" target="note.ledgerPage1" category="page" title="Ledger, page one">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: A torn page, numbered 1 in the top corner. A column of names, all struck through, and one bed number circled so hard the pen went through: 2.
</entry>

<entry id="ledgerPage2" on="read" target="note.ledgerPage2" category="page" title="Ledger, page two">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Page 2, soft with damp. Under the last name, a circled bed: 7. Someone has written beside it, AND STILL HE COMES.
</entry>

<entry id="ledgerPage3" on="read" target="note.ledgerPage3" category="page" title="Ledger, page three">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Page 3. Only one entry, and a bed number circled: 5. At the foot of the page: THE GATE REMEMBERS THEM IN ORDER.
  <match on="entry.ledgerPage1.read">
    <when is="true">
      @nell{code="0010" mono}: Two. Seven. And five. Page by page.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @nell{code="0020" mono}: In order. Then there are other pages.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</entry>

<entry id="orderlyFile" on="read" target="note.orderlyFile" category="file" title="Staff file: A. Crane">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: CRANE, Albert. Orderly, 1961 to 1979. Married. Reliable. Never late for the three o'clock round.
  @narrator{code="0020"}: 1968: course of electroconvulsive therapy at his own request. Since treatment, marked photophobia. Will not abide a lamp in his face.
  @narrator{code="0030"}: 1979: missing after the fire in the east stair. Not found. The round continues to be walked.
  @nell{code="0010" mono}: Will not abide a lamp. Toby's lantern.
</entry>

<entry id="diary" on="read" target="note.diary" category="file" title="Dr. Hale's diary">
  @hale{code="0010" vo}: 3rd November, 1979. The Board closes us Friday. They ask where the patients will go. The patients will not go. They are admitted. It is written.
  @hale{code="0020" vo}: As long as the ledger stands, they are ours. As long as the bell calls the round at three, Crane walks it. I have tried to stop the bell. I cannot stop the bell.
  @hale{code="0030" vo}: Burn the ledger, ring him down at three, and let them sleep. I am too much of a coward, and too much of a doctor.
</entry>
